#47 item 4: a recompute summary carries `targets_checked`, `targets_matched`
and digests -- and no `turns`. This is the issue's own acceptance row.

`turns: 0` is the honest spelling of the sentinel the ruling refuses: a
recompute counted no turns, so any number here means "not applicable" and
reads as a count. It is refused as an unknown key rather than by a check for
0 or -1, because the way to refuse a sentinel is to leave nowhere to put one.
